Merges into `<BRANCH>` are governed server-side by the branch ruleset
(`.github/rulesets/<file>.json` — the JSON is the source of truth; the live
ruleset is applied from it, and policy changes are PRs to that file).

- **Two things gate a merge, nothing else:**
  1. `merge-gate` — green only when every CI suite this PR's diff requires
     has succeeded on the head SHA. No path filter; it runs on every PR.
  2. `<agent-infra-guard | code-owner review>` — <agent-pattern> branches
     cannot touch protected infra surfaces (<list them>); those changes land
     from a human branch.
- **Required approvals: 0.** CI green = mergeable. Every bot review
  (<list your advisory reviewers>) is advisory — address findings on merit,
  but no bot can block a merge, and none should be waited on when
  rate-limited (skipped-and-noted, never waited-on).
- **No direct pushes to `<BRANCH>`**, no force-pushes, no branch deletion —
  admins included. There are no bypass actors.
- **Agent draft PRs flip ready automatically** when every workflow for the
  head SHA is green and no reviewer has requested changes
  (auto-ready workflow). <If staged CI: drafts run the fast lane only; the
  full suite and the real merge-gate evaluation fire at the flip.>
- **Break-glass** (gate wedged by something outside the diff): disable the
  ruleset → fix → re-enable → write it up. Runbook: <path>. Never merge past
  a red gate by editing the required-check list.
- **Dispatch convention:** at most 2–3 agent PRs in flight.
